From 67b2bfb5f02e8d89f0e3ab1877b3648d399611b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:18:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 43/63] glm cuda: a begin that fails after its step frees the
 slot on every rank; a request at --context opens

The round-3 reviews' four findings (opt/codex-round3.md, opt/deepseek-paged-review.md), each with host tests:

- P1, TP ranks left inconsistent: Leader.beginOn sends the begin step (with the stream's page ids), then runs rank 0's
  own begin. When that failed (a lazy DFlash2 ring allocation, a reset's memset), the lanes' opening released the slot
  on rank 0 alone, so a follower kept it mapped and the next begin on it was BadStep, ending the TP server. Rank 0's
  begin failing after its step went out now sends a release step for the slot: every rank frees it as rank 0 does.
  The follower's step handler moves into follow.apply (the loop is unchanged), so a host test drives the real one.
- A thin model with no paged caches (KDA layers alone, no target MTP head: TF_GLM_LAYERS=1 with --no-drafts or
  DFlash2) gave a zero-byte page, and the pool's plan divided by it. Engine.init keeps every stream's window when the
  loaded layers have nothing to page (pages.pageable), on every rank alike; pages.layout refuses such a model by name
  (error.NoPagedCaches) instead of reaching the plan.
- A request of exactly --context was refused: the opening refused prompt + max_tokens + a window equal to the capacity
  (capacity = context + 8 rounded up to 64, so whenever context + 8 is a multiple of 64), and prefillStart refused a
  prompt whose first window ends at the capacity. Both allow equality now (Lanes.fitsContext, Engine.promptFits), as
  does the batched prompts' check; the last window's rows still end inside the capacity.
- A checkpoint without an MTP layer (num_nextn_predict_layers 0), drafts on and no --drafter, selected the MTP head,
  loaded nothing, then failed every draft with NoDraftHead. engine.heads now loads no head and turns speculation off
  there (one warning on rank 0); DFlash2 still borrows the draft head (the rank's lm_head rows) without an MTP layer.

Tests (mutations of each fix fail them): test-glm-fp8-pages-host 15/15 (a begin failing after its step: rank 0's
steps are recorded off its link and replayed through follow.apply on a follower; a request of 8,000 + 184 at
--context 8,184 opens, + 185 is PromptTooLong), test-glm-kv-pages-host 25/25 (thin model; exact-context checks at six
contexts), test-glm-fp8-kv-host 20/20 (engine.heads).

